,"Getting Started","Featured"],"contentType":"quickstart","url":"https://quickstarts.snowflake.com/guide/tasty_bytes_zero_to_snowflake_collaboration_ptbr/index.html","summary":"Quickstart Tasty Bytes: do zero ao Snowflake - colaboração","lastUpdatedAt":"2024-09-12T11:16:58-07:00"},{"duration":10,"title":"Tasty Bytes: do zero ao Snowflake - dados semiestruturados","categories":["Tasty Bytes","Getting Started","Featured"],"contentType":"quickstart","url":"https://quickstarts.snowflake.com/guide/tasty_bytes_zero_to_snowflake_semi_structured_data_ptbr/index.html","summary":"Quickstart Tasty Bytes: do zero ao Snowflake - dados semiestruturados","lastUpdatedAt":"2024-09-12T11:16:58-07:00"},{"duration":10,"title":"Tasty Bytes: do zero ao Snowflake - transformação","categories":["Tasty Bytes","Getting Started","Featured"],"contentType":"quickstart","url":"https://quickstarts.snowflake.com/guide/tasty_bytes_zero_to_snowflake_transformation_ptbr/index.html","summary":"Quickstart Tasty Bytes: do zero ao Snowflake - transformação","lastUpdatedAt":"2024-09-12T11:16:58-07:00"},{"duration":41,"title":"Tasty Bytes: introdução ao Snowpark para ciência de dados","categories":["Tasty Bytes","Getting Started","Featured","Data Science \u0026 ML"],"contentType":"quickstart","url":"https://quickstarts.snowflake.com/guide/tasty_bytes_snowpark_101_for_data_science_ptbr/index.html","summary":"Tasty Bytes: introdução ao Snowpark para ciência de dados","lastUpdatedAt":"2024-09-12T11:16:58-07:00"},{"duration":41,"title":"Terraforming Snowflake","categories":["Featured","Getting Started","App Development","DevOps"],"contentType":"quickstart","url":"https://quickstarts.snowflake.com/guide/terraforming_snowflake/index.html","summary":"Learn how to manage Snowflake using Terraform","lastUpdatedAt":"2024-09-12T11:16:58-07:00"},{"duration":12,"title":"Text Embedding As A Snowpark Python UDF","categories":["Data Science \u0026 ML"],"contentType":"quickstart","url":"https://quickstarts.snowflake.com/guide/text_embedding_as_snowpark_python_udf/index.html","summary":"Text Embedding As A Snowpark Python UDF","lastUpdatedAt":"2024-09-12T11:16:58-07:00"},{"duration":48,"title":"Threat Intelligence on Snowflake Setup Guide","categories":["Cybersecurity"],"contentType":"quickstart","url":"https://quickstarts.snowflake.com/guide/Vulnerability Intelligence on Snowflake/index.html","summary":"This guide will walk you through how to load sample security data info Snowflake tables and then join the data meaningfully and present that information using a Streamlit frontend.","lastUpdatedAt":"2024-09-12T11:16:58-07:00"},{"duration":43,"title":"Tokenization in Snowflake Using Python UDFs (Python Camouflage)","categories":["Cybersecurity","Architecture Patterns","Solution Examples"],"contentType":"quickstart","url":"https://quickstarts.snowflake.com/guide/python_camouflage/index.html","summary":"Project Python Camouflage aims to give a working MVP for tokenization in Snowflake using Python. The problem this aims to solve is allowing customers to obfuscate (or “mask”) PII while at the same time not losing the ability to use that data in joins and other operations where the consistency of the data through operations is required. Python offers libraries to achieve this using encryption, and through the use of Snowflake Python UDFs we can apply that to information in Snowflake natively. As an MVP, this is not meant to offer a complete solution to the problem. Rather, this is a framework that others can embrace and extend.","lastUpdatedAt":"2024-09-12T11:16:58-07:00"},{"duration":34,"title":"Train an XGBoost Model with GPUs using Snowflake Notebooks","categories":["Data Science","Data Science \u0026 ML","Getting Started","Notebooks"],"contentType":"quickstart","url":"https://quickstarts.snowflake.com/guide/train-an-xgboost-model-with-gpus-using-snowflake-notebooks/index.html","summary":"This is a sample Snowflake Guide","lastUpdatedAt":"2024-09-12T11:16:58-07:00"},{"duration":0,"title